<article class="env-remark" id="06K7">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06K7">Remark <span data-tag="06K7">90.21.5</span>.</a> Hence a representable groupoid in functors on $\mathcal{C}$ is given by objects $U$ and $R$ of $\mathcal{C}$ and morphisms $s, t : U \to R$ and $c : R \to R \amalg _{s, U, t} R$ such that $(\underline{U}, \underline{R}, s, t, c)$ satisfies the condition of Definition <a href="/tag/06K3" data-tag="06K3">90.21.1</a>. The reason for requiring the existence of the pushout $R \amalg _{s, U, t} R$ is so that the composition morphism $c$ is defined at the level of morphisms in $\mathcal{C}$. This requirement will always be satisfied below when we consider representable groupoids in functors on $\widehat{\mathcal{C}}_\Lambda $, since by Lemma <a href="/tag/06SB" data-tag="06SB">90.4.3</a> the category $\widehat{\mathcal{C}}_\Lambda $ admits pushouts. </p>
</article>